{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The sense of <b>At the end of seven years you shall make a release.</b> [It is] at the beginning of the year, as I explained. And the witness is \"assemble the people,\" and this pericope is joined to it [the preceding one] because it says that the tithe of the poor is for the Levite and for the stranger and for the orphan and for the widow; so it says, and likewise the matter of the remission. And the sense is like \"remise it and leave it,\" and it falls [due]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is terse and elliptical throughout; the antecedents of several clauses are implied rather than stated. I have translated hyper-literally without supplying connective tissue. The clause 'ותפול' (\"and it falls\") is cryptic and may refer to the debt falling due or lapsing; left untranslated as to precise reference."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:30.478796124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}